<entry main-word="Aard-vark" source="1913 Webster;;WordNet 1.5">
<p>
<hw>Aard"-vark`</hw> <pos>n.</pos>
<def>A burrowing <it>African mammal</it> with a long snout that feeds chiefly on ants and termites.</def><br/
<altsp>[Spelled also <asp>Aardvark</asp>.]</altsp><br/
<syn><b>Syn.</b> -- ant bear, anteater.</syn><br/
</p>
<p>
<sn>2.</sn>
<cd>A second historical sense retained under the same lexical entry.</cd><br/
</p>
</entry>

<entry main-word="Aard-wolf" source="1913 Webster;;WordNet 1.5">
<p>
<hw>Aard"-wolf`</hw> <pos>n.</pos>
<def>A carnivorous, striped, quadruped mammal (<spn>Proteles cristata</spn>) of South Africa, resembling the fox and hyena.</def><br/
<altname>Aardwolf</altname><br/
<syn><b>Syn.</b> -- <it>earth-wolf</it>, maanhaar.</syn><br/
</p>
</entry>
